In the UK, the Joint Academic NETwork (JANET) has decided to drop all 
the alt.sex.* usenet groups from their news servers. Janet machines 
(suffix *.ac.uk) are the UK equivalent of the .edu domain in the USA.

Previously, only the alt.binaries groups were being censored at the 
University of Kent, and then only for posts containing UUEncoded data. 
Almost certainly aa follow-on from the finding of a porn archive at a 
midlands university, the whole hierarchy has now been cut off. Recently 
introduced legislation also makes it illegal for anyone to import 
pornography into the UK via telephone lines*, and this may be used to 
force commercial UK service providers to drop the hierarchy as well, if 
UUEncoded pics 9or even the textual content of the groups) is ruled 
indecent (not necessarily obscene).

* There is some doubt as to whether a fiber-optic line constitutes a 
"telephone" line in UK law. This is one possible derailment; the other 
is to go through the European courts, but the test case is likely to be 
expensive and very long indeed.

	Baphomet

