When the fat pipe first opened, and academic sites in Europe found
themselves getting the whole of Usenet for the first time, it only took a
few days before the main gateway site to JANET sites in the UK decided
not to transmit alt.sex.*, alt.drugs, and rec.arts.erotica, and that was
precisely their justification.  A flamewar erupted on uk.news ("A degree
of spinelessness that would be shaming in a jellyfish" etc.), but the
policy stuck.  Other sites were free to do as they wished, but that one
site was at the time the only cheap way to get most of the non-technical
newsgroups.

I guess the PTB have only just realised that with the growth of the
Internet, everyone that wanted to eventually became able to bypass that
site.

