>What is the recently introduced legislation to which you refer, please?

It is the misnamed Criminal Justice Act 1994 -- the same Act that makes it 
a criminal offence to trespass on private land, even "common" land, which 
makes "rave" parties illegal and which makes it illegal for gypsies and 
other travelling people to congregate in groups of more than three vehicles. 

That such may be in breach of European legislation, or even the Universal 
Declaration on Human Rights seems not to concern our "lords and masters".

It is perfect proof of the maxim that "hard cases make bad law", for that 
rotten law was made by some of the hardest cases ever to be elected.

As there is some doubt as to whether text-based material and, in particular, 
simple discussion of the various topics involved, would constitute 
"pornography", the actions by the JANET heirarchy may well be a considerable 
over-reaction to the legislation. It's more likely, IMCO, that they're 
merely using that as an excuse or rationalisation for a disinclination to 
participate fully in Usenet

