I love your signature file, but I find that resolute wickedness
in this country is a rather stale affair constructed from second-
hand wisdom, rather than learned on one's own, which is by far
the more creative path to go.  In other words, those fools who
mistake their `training' for wisdom don't realise what adventures
they have missed.

As for the lilt of the article, I assure you that my `WinVM' mail
reader decoded it instantly and deposited the decoded version in
the directory of my choosing.  You just click on the File menu
button and click again on `Decode Article'.  I have the misfortune
of being able to express myself in writing, even after getting a
ph. d. in engineering, so I forget that my less gifted bretheren
sometimes lack the adventure to try new keyboard and mouse com-
binations.  Still, if you are desperate to know what the decoded
article says, just look in soc.rights.human.

BTW, where are all the brave liberals whose tongues are tied when
they see a videotape on television news of a nearly crippled
homeless man waving a knife taped to his arm (because he was
incapable of grasping it), and being shot to death by a platoon
of Capital Park Police?  I know from personal experience that
the Park Police in Washington, D. C., don't like to get their
uniforms dirty when ordinary citizens are being molested and 
mugged in broad daylight at noontime.  And, to listen to their
supervisor exonerating this murder is enough to provoke nausea.


